---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Fire Risk Assessments Scotland"
  description="Fire risk assessments for commercial, residential and mixed-use premises across Scotland. Clear inspections, practical reporting and next-step compliance support."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="section-title">Fire Risk Assessments in Scotland</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Practical fire risk assessments for landlords, property managers, businesses and duty holders across Scotland. We help identify fire safety risks, record the findings clearly and set out sensible next steps for compliance.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quote">Request a fire risk assessment</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Who needs a fire risk assessment?</h2>
      <p>
        Fire risk assessments are commonly required for non-domestic premises, workplaces, commercial buildings, common-use areas, HMOs, holiday lets, care-related properties and other premises where fire safety duties apply. In Scotland, duty holders are expected to manage fire safety risks and keep suitable arrangements in place.
      </p>
      <p>
        Typical clients include landlords, letting agents, facilities managers, business owners, housing providers, developers and property teams preparing buildings for occupation, lease, sale or compliance review.
      </p>

      <h2>What is included?</h2>
      <p>
        Our assessment looks at the building, its use, the people who may be at risk and the fire safety measures already in place. The report is designed to be clear, practical and useful for decision-making rather than filled with unnecessary jargon.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Review of fire hazards and ignition risks</li>
        <li>Assessment of escape routes and means of escape</li>
        <li>Review of fire detection, warning and emergency lighting arrangements</li>
        <li>Checks on fire doors, compartmentation and general fire precautions where visible</li>
        <li>Consideration of occupancy, building use and vulnerable persons</li>
        <li>Prioritised action points with practical recommendations</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Fire risk assessment reports for Scottish properties</h2>
      <p>
        After the visit, you receive a written fire risk assessment report outlining the key findings, risk areas and recommended actions. This can support internal compliance records, landlord obligations, managing agent files, insurance requests or wider property due diligence.
      </p>

      <h2>Types of premises we can support</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Offices, shops and commercial units</li>
        <li>Rental properties and managed property portfolios</li>
        <li>HMOs and premises with sleeping accommodation</li>
        <li>Industrial, storage and workshop premises</li>
        <li>Community, leisure and mixed-use buildings</li>
        <li>Property transactions, refurbishments and change-of-use projects</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>FAQs</h2>

      <h3>How quickly can this be arranged?</h3>
      <p>
        Timescales depend on the property location, building size, access arrangements and the urgency of the instruction. If you have a deadline, tell us when requesting a quote and we will confirm availability.
      </p>

      <h3>Is a fire risk assessment a legal requirement in Scotland?</h3>
      <p>
        For many non-domestic and relevant premises, Scottish fire safety law places duties on those responsible for fire safety to assess and manage fire risk. The Scottish Fire and Rescue Service also states that duty holders are responsible for carrying out fire risk assessments for relevant premises.
      </p>

      <h3>Do you cover all of Scotland?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. We support clients across Glasgow, Edinburgh, central Scotland and wider Scottish locations depending on the property type, access and project requirements.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/services">Explore related services</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Book a fire risk assessment</h2>
      <p>
        Send us the property address, building type and reason for the assessment, and we will confirm the scope, timescale and cost.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quote">Get a quote</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>